Regarding the first problem of yours that you describe in that post, 
setting the Boolean option "travel" to "false" will turn off the feature 
that didn't go well with your laptop design (I can totally understand 
the annoyance). However, a mouse-click will still mean an attempt to 
take one step in the direction of the clicked point.

From the built-in help texts:
"travel - enable the command to travel to a map location via a shortest-
path algorithm, usually invoked by '_'"

There might also be a way to turn off mouse input and keep the '_' 
functionality, I'm not sure though.

